Intellego bundles and downloads data from the RUAccent project
(https://github.com/Den4ikAI/ruaccent, https://huggingface.co/ruaccent/accentuator),
licensed under the MIT License:

  Stress and ё dictionaries (assets/dict, generated by tool/build_dictionaries.py)
  ONNX models (downloaded at runtime by lib/features/nlp/accent/onnx/model_store.dart)

The Dart pipeline in lib/features/nlp/accent/onnx is a port of RUAccent's
Python pipeline.

Speech recognition for reading aloud uses the GigaAM-v2 Russian CTC model by
SaluteDevices (https://github.com/salute-developers/GigaAM, MIT License, v2 was
released under MIT in December 2024), in the int8 ONNX export published by the
sherpa-onnx project (https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx, Apache License 2.0),
which also provides the runtime (package sherpa_onnx). The model is downloaded
at runtime by lib/features/speaking/asr_model_store.dart.
